# Negative test: within the GMN math plane (@μ, selected by the denotation context
# gmeow:gmnMathGlyphContext), a single operator — one lang:denotationTarget — MUST bind
# ONE consistent precedence. If the same target has two infix forms declaring DIFFERENT
# gmeow:gmnPrecedence values, its binding strength is undecidable and a downstream
# operator-precedence parser cannot place it in the ladder. Any returned row is that
# violation.
#
# This is the precedence-CONSISTENCY complement to gmn-form-signature-completeness.rq
# (which checks only that a fixity-bearing form HAS a precedence). It deliberately does
# NOT flag distinct operators sharing one precedence band: that is by design (∈ ⊆ < >
# ≤ ≥ ⊇ all sit at the relational band 50; the additive band is 60, multiplicative 70),
# and cross-operator band-sharing is resolved by associativity, not precedence. The only
# genuine clash a precedence gate can prove from data is a single operator carrying two
# precedences — an operator clashing with itself — so that is exactly what this flags.
#
# The current math-plane population binds each operator target to one infix form at one
# precedence, so this query returns no rows.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/>

SELECT ?target ?formA ?formB ?precA ?precB WHERE {
    ?denA lang:denotationContext gmeow:gmnMathGlyphContext ;
          lang:denotationTarget ?target ;
          lang:denotedForm ?formA .
    ?denB lang:denotationContext gmeow:gmnMathGlyphContext ;
          lang:denotationTarget ?target ;
          lang:denotedForm ?formB .
    ?formA gmeow:gmnFixity gmeow:gmnFixityInfix ;
           gmeow:gmnPrecedence ?precA .
    ?formB gmeow:gmnFixity gmeow:gmnFixityInfix ;
           gmeow:gmnPrecedence ?precB .
    FILTER (STR(?formA) < STR(?formB))
    FILTER (?precA != ?precB)
}
ORDER BY ?target ?formA ?formB
